# Rust
/target/
**/target/
debug/
release/
*.rs.bk
*.rlib
*.prof*
# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED, not ignored. `bee` ships a binary, so the lock is the
# reproducible-build record — and CI has no other pin: it resolves from scratch on a
# clean runner. Leaving it out broke CI when `bisync` (every version, via
# gix-protocol <- gix =0.86.0) was yanked from crates.io; a committed lock keeps
# resolving because cargo honours a yanked version already recorded in it.

# eBPF build artifacts
*.o
*.bpf.o

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.tmp

# Env / logs
*.log
.env*

# Scanner scratch reports (016-native-tools): a scanner child writes its SARIF here and
# `bee sarif-worker` consumes it in the same call. Transient by construction.
#
# `.bee/findings/` is deliberately NOT ignored — the finding ledger is meant to be committed,
# diffed, and reviewed in a pull request (FR-023, Constitution IV).
.bee/scan/

# Python bytecode (the VM gates import validate_results.py)
__pycache__/
